  "figure": {
    "caption": "Linear search (cow path): a robot starts at the origin of a line and must reach a target at unknown distance $d \\ge 1$ on an unknown side. The animation runs the doubling strategy at unit speed, turning at $1, -2, 4, -8, \\dots$ (trace above the line, one level per trip); the target, at $d = 2.5$ just beyond the turning point $-2$, is found on the next trip to the left at time $16.5 = 6.6\\,d$. In the worst case the strategy finds the target within time $9d$, which is optimal [BaezaYates1993Searching].",
